<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Does It Make Sense 2021 source-based teaching"><h2>Warm-up — Is It Greater?</h2><p>132+115=247, so above 200: true. 228+195=423, so above400: true. 217+151=368, so above400: false. Explain why without relying only on the calculator.</p><h2>Activity 1 — Quick Estimates</h2><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Original character</th><th>Changes</th><th>Exact</th><th>Reasonable mental check</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Priya</td><td>212−98+308</td><td>422</td><td>About400, yes</td></tr><tr><td>Clare</td><td>252−92+203</td><td>363</td><td>About360</td></tr><tr><td>Han</td><td>558+302−250</td><td>610</td><td>About610</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Activity 2 — Solve and Reason</h2><p>Jada: 326−32−84=<strong>210</strong>. Noah: 624+132+48=<strong>804</strong>. Select one, show the method, exchange with a partner and discuss whether both answers make sense. The teacher reviews estimates and reasoning.</p><p>Publisher's wood bead photograph and gated Beads in the Bin Cool-down are not reproduced. Edulytics has independent goal-equivalent practice only.</p><p><a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-3/lesson-17/lesson.html">2021 original source lesson</a></p></section>